 "title": "CDC Datasets",
 "hook": "This week we're exploring datasets that the Trump administration has purged. The Trump administration has ordered agencies to purge their websites of any references to topics such as LGBTQ+ rights. An effort is underway to back up this publicly funded data before it is lost. This week's dataset contains metadata about CDC datasets backed up on archive.org. \"The removal of HIV- and LGBTQ-related resources from the websites of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention and other health agencies is deeply concerning and creates a dangerous gap in scientific information and data to monitor and respond to disease outbreaks,\" the Infectious Disease Society of America said in a statement.",
 "questions": [
